    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #50989.\n\nWhen a tool has `strict: true` and empty parameters (`\"properties\": {}, \"required\": [], \"additionalProperties\": false`), xgrammar generates a degenerate grammar `root ::= [ \\n\\t]*` — whitespace-only with no exit condition. The model loops on whitespace tokens indefinitely (doom loop).\n\n**Fix** (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py`):\n- For vLLM-defined structural tags (hermes, minimax, etc.): `get_function_parameters()` returns `True` (unconstrained) when the schema has no properties, avoiding the degenerate grammar.\n- For xgrammar-builtin structural tags (Qwen, DeepSeek): `_dump_tool_for_xgrammar()` omits `strict: true` when parameters have no properties, so xgrammar uses unconstrained argument generation.\n\nThe model already knows to output `{}` for no-argument tools — the grammar was the obstacle.\n\n## Test Results\n\n**Unit tests (CPU):** 11/11 custom tests + 267/267 existing tests (`test_structural_tag_registry.py`) passed.\n\n**GPU E2E tests (`Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`, 1x H100):** 5/5 passed\n- Empty-properties strict tool: 89 tokens, 0.56s, `finish_reason=stop` (no doom loop)\n- Completion time check: 0.56s vs 60s+ timeout without fix\n- Non-empty strict tool: no regression\n- Streaming with empty-properties tool: 88 SSE chunks, `finish_reason=stop`\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] Custom unit tests for empty-properties detection and grammar bypass\n- [x] Existing `test_structural_tag_registry.py` tests pass (267/267)\n- [x] GPU E2E test with Qwen3-0.6B confirms no doom loop\n\n## Notes\n\n- Only affects tools with `strict: true` and zero properties — non-empty schemas are unchanged.\n- `_has_no_properties()` checks for no `properties` AND no `additionalProperties`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
